 "findings": [
  "Conductors and ducts: 4.9 t for three 3 kV sectors (739 mm2 Al per pole), feeders, nine normally-open ties, the 10 kV L1 bus, the 6 kV defense bus and the refuge bus; the Phase VI distribution line is 8.0 t (covers it). Bus loss 27 kW at full load (a WARM load).",
  "Single faults: 7 of 8 ride through with storage; the district-loss case is the design case for the refuge.",
  "Storage: Ride-through cells (4 per sector) OK (restored in 26 s (Phase V transient)); Main battery (EPS-A, canon) OK (shared main bus); Restart pack R1b (one per unit) OK (own cells, converter and start bus; never tied to the refuge); Defense buffer (4 modules) OK (10 s burst; recharge 43 s from the 4.8 MW L2 surplus); Survival bridge (refuge) OK (5 h at 50 kW; L3 start 4 h assumed (type OPEN)).",
  "Separation: BUS-1/L1 0.93 m -> arc/fire barrier + separate cable trays; DATA-A/NaK-U3R 1.28 m -> acceptable (> 1 m); 1000 K line: multi-foil insulation and a thermal barrier; DATA-B/NaK-U1S 1.28 m -> acceptable (> 1 m); 1000 K line: multi-foil insulation and a thermal barrier.",
  "L3 stays a type-OPEN refuge source (radioisotope-Stirling or fuel cell, Phase IV); it has its own bus and no tie to the main buses (owner rule)."
